WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.060
If you want to hear how Coraline's early childhood
experiences helped her survive and save her

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.360
parents later on, then stick around to the
end of this video.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.500
[INTRO]

00:00:11.509 --> 00:00:15.509
The Other Mother was an evil entity who preyed
on the souls of children living in a particular

00:00:15.509 --> 00:00:19.170
house for hundreds of years, and after a long
reign of manipulation and terror, there was

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:23.109
only one girl who was able to outwit her and
finally put an end to the horrors that took

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:24.109
place there.

00:00:24.109 --> 00:00:27.890
Welcome to Horror History, in today’s lesson
I’m analysing the life of Coraline Jones,

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:31.630
the brave explorer who was the first to ever
survive the wonders of an alternate realm

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.239
called The Other World.

00:00:33.239 --> 00:00:36.900
In order to understand where Coraline got the strength
needed to take down the Other Mother, we first

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.900
need to take things back to the beginning.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:44.700
[HORROR HISTORY]

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:48.420
Coraline Jones was born as the only daughter
of two loving parents named Mel and Charlie

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.480
in the movie, but who are not named in the
book.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.160
Although they do care for Coraline, they are
oftentimes very busy with their work; both of them

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.060
work from home on computers and I’ve never
related to two characters so hard before.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:06.100
Coraline’s favorite pastime was to go out
exploring, but the house that the Jones’s

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:10.030
live in is in a bad part of town, where people
throw away their unwanted junk, so her parents

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.060
forbid her from exploring in that area.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:15.420
Coraline is persistent about though, and one
day her Dad agrees to go with her, and they

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.520
come across a stream at the bottom of a hill.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.280
Mr. Jones tells her to run up the hill as
fast as she could, and she obeys as he stays

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.280
behind.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.740
When she got back to the top of the hill,
he runs up after her and picks her up.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.990
He would later explain that the air was filled
with wasps, and he had stayed back to take

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.409
the stings in order to give her time to escape.

00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:32.880
He would explain to her that he didn’t see
the action as bravery.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:36.619
"It wasn't brave because he wasn't scared:
it was the only thing he could do.

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:39.930
But going back again to get his glasses, when
he knew the wasps were there, when he was

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:40.979
really scared.

00:01:40.979 --> 00:01:41.979
That was brave."

00:01:41.979 --> 00:01:45.110
This scene not only shows how much her father
actually cares for her, but it would give

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.369
her the bravery she needed later in the story.

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:50.500
She also learned the value of resilience as
a child, when her mother first took the training

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:54.619
wheels off her bicycle and she ended up getting
scrapes on top of scrapes, but had a sense

00:01:54.619 --> 00:01:56.399
of achievement when she finally mastered it.

00:01:56.399 --> 00:01:58.509
Coraline had an otherwise normal childhood.

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:02.670
She came to find that she had an intense discomfort
around spiders and she enjoyed eating simple

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:06.500
foods, and wasn’t a fan of her father’s
complicated recipes, like his "leek and potato

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.130
stew, with a tarragon garnish and melted Gruyére
cheese."

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:11.490
She was also not a fan of coconut.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:14.500
When Coraline’s grandmother passed away,
she left all of her expensive furniture to

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.810
the family, which Coraline found very uncomfortable,
but it didn’t matter because she wasn’t

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:20.080
allowed to play in the drawing room where
it was kept anyway.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:23.300
The main story takes place one summer, three
weeks before the beginning of school.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.300
We know that this isn’t her first year of
school, because it mentions that she’s been

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:30.130
there multiple times before, so I’d guess
she’s going into second or third grade.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:33.800
The family moved into a new house just outside
of London, which was in a much safer area for

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:35.440
Coraline to explore and play in.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:37.040
The Joneses owned only part of the house.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.640
They were above Miss Spink and Miss Forcible, who were
on the ground floor, and below Mr. Bobo who was on

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:42.640
the top floor.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.600
There was also a unit adjacent to them on
the second floor, which was vacant at the

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:46.620
time they moved in.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.980
One of the first discoveries that Coraline
makes upon moving in is the door to the vacant

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.790
flat, which filled her with intrigue.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:55.000
The door was locked, and on one rainy day,
Mrs. Jones shows her that there’s only a

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.120
brick wall behind it, which was likely put
up when the house was divided up.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:01.650
The next day, as she’s setting out to go
explore, Mr. Bobo from upstairs tells her

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:05.250
that the mice he’s supposedly training for
his jumping mouse circus have a message for

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.080
her, telling her: don’t go through the door.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.280
This seems to suggest that animals are privy
to the Other World in a way that other people

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.500
are not, which we see later with The Cat.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.401
Coraline sets out to find a well that Miss
Spink and Miss Forcible told her about, which

00:03:15.401 --> 00:03:19.330
is supposedly very deep and very dangerous,
and Coraline finds this kind of exciting because

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.230
she finds everything else boring.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:24.440
School is only a week away now, and it’s
raining outside, so Coraline stays in and

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.800
draws an abstract picture which looks like
this.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.541
The “I” is lost in the mist, a forewarning
about how she would soon be lost in The Other

00:03:30.541 --> 00:03:31.541
World.

00:03:31.541 --> 00:03:34.450
Another warning comes when she visits the
old ladies down stairs and they read her tea

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.240
leaves to predict she’ll be in danger.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:40.700
With no siblings or friends to play with, she thinks a
little danger would be some welcome excitement.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:44.400
Miss Spink suggests that she “Never wear
green in your dressing room,” and Coraline

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.790
has no idea what that means, and I didn’t
either at first, so let’s break it down.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:51.290
Miss Spink’s main thing is that she’s
a retired theatre actress, so she’s referencing

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:54.730
an old theatre superstition that the performers
shouldn’t wear green, because it’s bad

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.880
luck and it was thought that they would not
stand out from the background which consisted

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.490
of green trees, grass and bushes.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:03.320
Coraline however, while shopping for school
clothes later in the story, wants to buy a

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:07.070
green pair of gloves to make her stand out
from her classmates, and it would ultimately

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:10.840
be her alternative way of thinking that got
her out of a few scary situations.

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:14.350
Miss Spink and Miss Forcible also give her
a stone with a hole in it, which they believe

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:15.790
might help her in some way.

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:19.560
One afternoon, while she’s once again terribly
bored of her life, her mom goes out to get

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:23.150
food for lunch and Coraline opens the door
in the drawing room, but instead of a wall

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.060
of bricks, there’s a hallway.

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:28.940
It leads to an almost identical version of
her world, but certain things look more sinister,

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:32.180
like the picture of the boy in the drawing
room, who is normally staring at some bubbles,

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:35.380
but not looks like he’s planning to do something
very nasty to them.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:39.580
“Let’s get this over with so I can go
home and play my clarinet.”

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:43.790
Coraline meets her Other Mother, who is like
Coraline’s real mother but has buttons for

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:46.780
eyes and has much more interest in paying
attention to Coraline.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:49.270
They have a lunch with food that Coraline
actually really likes.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:53.360
“‘We've been waiting for you for a long
time,’ said Coraline's other father.”

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:54.120
Yep.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.480
Typically not a great idea to talk to people
who say that.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:00.040
They tell her that everyone has a set of Other
parents, she just never knew about hers until

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.040
now.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:03.780
The rats upstairs sing and perform for her,
which she finds a little off putting, but

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.470
is willing to look past it because at least
it’s something interesting.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:09.410
She goes out to explore and finds that the
cat in the garden can talk now.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:13.210
He tells her he’s the same cat from her
world, and hints at the possibility of danger

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.240
in this world.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:28.070
The next wonder of the Other World that Coraline
visits is the location that usually contains

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:31.080
Miss Spink and Miss Forcible’s flat, which
is now a small theater.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:34.700
The audience is filled with talking dogs,
and the old ladies perform on unicycles on

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.990
stage, before stepping out of the old lady
suits and revealing they are actually thin

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:42.220
young women with black button eyes, perhaps
to resemble the ideal versions of Spink and

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:44.070
Forcible told about in their stories.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:47.730
Coraline volunteers to take part in a stunt
in which this Other Miss Forcible throws a

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:51.660
knife just above her head to pop a balloon,
and gets a box of chocolates as a reward.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:55.210
After finding out that the theater will continue
performing forever, she decides to leave,

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:57.290
and thinks it’s time to be getting back
to her own world.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:01.700
But before she goes, she runs into her other
parents, who are just... waiting for her there.

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:05.490
They tell her if she likes it here, she can
stay forever, she just has to sew these buttons

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:06.500
over her eyes.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:09.450
She basically NOPEs right out of there and
passes back through the door.

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:12.930
When she gets to the other side, the hallway
behind her is replaced by the brick wall before

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.160
she can turn back around.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:17.600
Her mom still hasn’t returned when she gets
back, so she watches TV as her parents are

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:18.600
gone all day.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.780
She asks the ladies downstairs about them,
but they haven’t seen anything, and are

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.620
about to take off to visit Miss Spink’s
niece.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:27.510
She goes to the supermarket to get her own
meal, which consisted of limeade, cake and

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:28.510
apples.

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:32.250
She wrote a story on her dad’s computer,
but at 3:12AM, her parents were still not

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:34.280
back, and she cried herself to sleep in their
bed.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:37.620
I think this is an important sequence, because
Coraline’s parents are gone and she has

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:41.090
free reign to do whatever she wants all the
time, but it isn’t as fulfilling as she

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:42.090
thought it would be.

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:45.260
Just as the Other World appears to be this
amazing place where everything is catered

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:49.060
towards pleasing her and she finds it has
it’s drawbacks, the real world is also less

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:50.650
fun without limitations.

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:52.720
I think we’ve all experienced this in some
form.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.720
When you’re old enough to buy your own groceries,
you don’t just buy your favorite food every

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.940
day, because then it’s not special when
you do have it.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:06:59.840
The next day she’s woken up by The Cat.

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:02.820
Being back in the real world, it doesn't
speak, but it leads her to her the mirror

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:06.910
downstairs, and in the reflection, she sees
her parents looking sad and alone.

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:10.040
Her mom leaves a message with her finger,
which says HELP US backwards.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:12.080
Coraline knows what she has to do.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:14.197
She gathers her bravery, marches up… and...

00:07:14.197 --> 00:07:16.960
calls the police, one of the funniest parts

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:17.960
of the book in my opinion.

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:21.400
Of course, they don’t take her seriously
at all, so then she brings a couple of apples

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:25.180
and the stone with a hole in it and heads
back to the Other World with the cat.

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:28.440
“What we do here is go back.”

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:36.260
The Other Mother is waiting for her there,
and tries to tell her that her parents gave

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:38.770
her the slip because they weren’t interested
in having her anymore.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:42.950
She has one of her rats steal the key to the
gateway door, thus trapping Coraline inside.

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:46.760
Her other parents go to bed, and the Cat suggests
that The Other Mother loves games, and maybe

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:50.230
if Coraline challenges her, she can win her
parents’ freedom back.

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:53.690
Coraline is terrified to sleep in the other
world, so she barricades her room using the

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.080
toybox before she goes to sleep.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:58.639
When she goes downstairs the next day, things
are getting even more weird than they were

00:07:58.639 --> 00:07:59.639
before.

00:07:59.639 --> 00:08:03.040
She goes to her Other Father’s study, and
finds him just standing there, kind of pretending

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.090
to work, but not actually getting anything
done.

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:08.460
She realizes that the house is mostly the
same as her house, but there are a few small

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:12.040
differences, like the snow globe on the drawing
room mantle which is usually empty.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:15.600
She also realizes that this other reality
is really just the house and the property

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.060
that immediately surrounds it.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:20.340
She figures out that this place was created
by the Other Mother to catch her like a spider

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:23.670
in a web, and that she hadn’t bothered to
create anything beyond what you could see

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:24.730
from the house.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:28.820
She notices that the trees further back in the distance
look worse and worse, and it gets more and

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:32.500
more misty, and she eventually walks all the
way around and back to the house, as if it

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:33.770
were all one large sphere.

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:36.790
This entire description reminds me of one
thing: a video game.

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:40.590
The Other Mother created this world to entice
Coraline and get her to want to stay forever,

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:43.130
just as a video game developer creates a fun
world for the player.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:46.020
But if you break outside the boundaries of
where you’re supposed to be, the developers

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:47.020
put less effort.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:50.580
The trees look very pixelated because you’re
not supposed to see this part up close, you’re

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:51.980
supposed to stay immersed in the game.

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:55.070
That’s what video game devs want, and that’s
what The Other Mother wants as well.

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:57.160
I think there’s a video game metaphor in
Coraline.

00:08:57.160 --> 00:09:00.700
It’s very similar to the favorite food analogy
I mentioned earlier, playing a video game

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:04.140
can be fun, but you don’t want to spend
all your time there and lose touch with the

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:05.140
real world.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:08.050
When Coraline gets back, the Other Mother
locks her behind the mirror for having poor

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:11.450
manners, and it is there where she meets the
ghosts of the other kids whose souls were

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:14.520
stolen, by The Other Mother, one of whom refers
to her as “The Beldam”.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:18.700
They tell her that the Beldam will take her
life, joy, heart and soul and leave her hollow.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.640
And yes, I’m aware that my logo resembles
the hollow mask from Bleach, you can stop

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:23.190
commenting that every day.

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:24.190
Every day…

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:27.020
The next day, Other Mother brings her back
through the mirror into the kitchen, and Coraline

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:28.180
challenges her to a bet.

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:31.430
If she can find the souls of the ghost children
and her parents, then the Other Mother must

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:32.430
let her go.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:36.120
Other Mother accepts, swearing her right hand
on it, but Coraline has no idea how she’s

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:39.210
actually going to find these things until
she sees her reflection in the mirror, where

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:43.160
the Adder Stone given to her by the old women
from downstairs is a glowing green coal.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:44.660
This gives her the idea to look through it.

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:45.360
"OK."

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:46.700
"Ready?"

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:47.320
"Yeah.."

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:49.320
"Here we go. See you Shane!"

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:50.460
"What?"

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:51.420
"OOH--"

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:53.800
And that is when little Coraline decided,
you know what?

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:55.100
I’m out.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:57.500
No.

00:09:57.510 --> 00:10:00.850
But she did find an ember colored marble
that emitted the voice of the ghost boy and

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:01.850
collected it.

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:05.380
Which by the way is another video game comparison,
I can’t tell you how many video games force you

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:10.260
to collect three spiritual stones, or 101
power cells… or whatever these things are.

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:11.900
"All I need to do is jump across this.

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:14.500
NO!!! YOU'VE GOTTA BE KIDDING M--"

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:17.710
So she gets the marble, and with each one
she gets, the world around her kind of starts

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:18.710
falling apart.

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:21.700
The next place she looks is in the theater,
where the book describes some of the most

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:24.300
horrific creatures ever created.

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:35.760
Coraline goes in search of the next soul in
the theater, which now abandoned and dusty.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.800
She casts a torch light upon the ceiling and
sees these dog-bat things.

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:42.490
They aren’t too scary in the film, but in
the book, they are described as hairless,

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:46.480
jellyish creatures that may have once been
dogs, but had wings and hung like bats or

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:47.120
spiders.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:50.780
There’s some kind of egg sac thing behind
the stage, which contains two heads and two

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.880
of each limb, and when viewed through the
stone, Coraline could see one of the souls

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:55.100
glowing inside.

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:59.190
So Coraline actually had to reach inside of
this thing, Bill Denbrough style and retrieve

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:00.820
it, but she accidentally wakes it up.

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:04.430
When she sees the face, I can’t even describe
it any better than it is in the book, so let

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.430
me just read that excerpt.

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:09.530
It resembled “the younger versions of Miss
Spink and Miss Forcible, but twisted and squeezed

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:14.380
together, like two lumps of wax that had melted
and melded together into one ghastly object.”

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:15.380
Yep.

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:16.570
That’s pretty messed up.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.570
One of the hands grabs out at her and starts
yelling at her, calling her a thief.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:22.790
As much as I love the movie, I’d kind of
like to see the David Cronenberg version of

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:25.560
this, mostly just so I can see his interpretation
of this scene.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:28.580
When she gets back out, the world is starting
to contort and lose it’s form.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:31.790
She tells Other Mother that she’s found
two of the three souls, and Other Mother tosses

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:34.120
her a key to the other second floor flat.

00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:37.010
Remember, this is the equivalent of the vacant
flat from Coraline’s world.

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:40.470
It’s her curiosity about that area that
got her into this whole mess, and it would

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.690
get her into trouble again here.

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:46.010
This is the most haunting location Coraline
ever has to explore.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:49.710
She finds a giant dead spider in the bath,
one of her worst fears, and eventually makes

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:51.959
it to a trap door leading into a cellar.

00:11:51.959 --> 00:11:55.339
When she gets down there and turns on the
light, she finds crude paintings on the wall,

00:11:55.339 --> 00:11:57.790
but the bulb was not bright enough to fully
make them out.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:12:00.910
There was a bad smell from a rubbish pile
in the corner, cardboard boxes covered in

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:04.220
mildew and decaying curtains, under which
she noticed… a pair of feet.

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:08.480
She comes to find that the feet belong to
a pale, puffy deformed blob that sits up and

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:09.970
stares at her with dark button eyes.

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:11.900
I would conclude that like everything

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:16.000
she has encountered in the Other World, The
Other Father seen had seen was only an illusion.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.800
She had manipulated this thing to look and
act like her Father in order to trick her,

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:22.220
and she had discarded it here when she was
done with it.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:26.081
I think maybe the creepiest part of this is
how when it speaks, “A mouth opens in the

00:12:26.081 --> 00:12:29.250
mouthless face and strands of pale stuff sticks
to the lips.”

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:33.300
This is also an important moment for Coraline’s
character development, because she tells herself,

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:34.430
“You can be brave.”

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:37.700
Which is a reference to the story about her
real dad getting stung my the wasps for her.

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:41.100
Now she’s got to find that same bravery
to maneuver her way out of this situation

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:42.580
and be the one to save him.

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:45.380
She gets out of the situation by pulling the
thing’s button off when it attacks her,

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:48.210
running for the trap door and locking the
abandoned flat when she escapes.

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:52.160
Her last place to look is the top flat, where
Mr. Bobo normally lives.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:55.600
In this world, there was no man up there,
just a horde of rats that give form to the

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:56.600
man’s clothes.

00:12:56.600 --> 00:13:00.450
She spots the last soul glowing in her viewfinder,
but it’s being taken away by one of the

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:01.450
rats.

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:04.230
Coraline gave chase, but ended up falling
on the stairs, and the rat appeared to get

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:08.060
away, but luckily for her, she had befriended
The Cat, and he’d captured it, earning her

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:09.190
the final soul.

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:12.500
Upon finding it, the house flattened even
more, until it looked like a charcoal scribble

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:16.589
on grey paper, and she quickly went into the
house to find her parents and confront the

00:13:16.589 --> 00:13:17.589
Other Mother.

00:13:17.589 --> 00:13:20.589
The ghost children speak to her through the
marbles, telling her that the Beldam won’t

00:13:20.589 --> 00:13:24.730
hold true to her word even if Coraline wins,
so she comes up with a cunning plan to outsmart

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:25.730
her.

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:28.370
After spending pretty much the entire adventure
thinking about it, Coraline realizes where

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:32.310
her parents are hidden: in the snow globe
on the mantle, the one major difference between

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:33.310
the two worlds.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:36.460
She tells the Other Mother she thinks they
are in the passageway between the worlds,

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:38.750
thus getting her to open it and prove her
wrong.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:41.580
Coraline grabs the snowglobe while her back
is turned, throws the cat, and is able to

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:45.230
escape back to her world, bringing her Mom
and Dad with her and freeing the souls of

00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:46.230
the children.

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:49.930
When she gets back home she appreciates her
world for what it is, we know she’s completed

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:53.370
her character transformation when she falls
asleep on the uncomfortable armchair in the

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:54.370
drawing room.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:57.351
Her father makes pineapple pizza for dinner,
which is kind of a compromise for her, she

00:13:57.351 --> 00:13:59.589
eats the pizza but leaves the pineapple chunks…

00:13:59.589 --> 00:14:01.600
The pineapple chunks are the only good part

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:09.180
That night, she dreamt of a picnic under an
old oak tree, where she played with the children

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:10.420
whose souls she had rescued.

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:13.890
It’s a sweet moment because she finally
has friends to play with in a way, but then

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:17.660
she thinks she sees a shadow cross over their
faces and they tell her there is more she

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:18.660
has to do.

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:22.650
The Other Mother had sworn by her right hand
let her go if she won the game, so now the

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:25.930
hand was scuttling around her world like a
spider, trying to steal back the key.

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:29.830
The next day, Coraline visits Miss Spink and
Miss Forcible again, and they tell her almost

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:33.440
everything is well, but they do see an ominous
hand in her future.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:36.570
Coraline comes up with one final plan to try
to do away with the Other Mother once and

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:37.570
for all.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:40.620
She sneaks back to the spot she had initially
set out to look for when they first moved

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:43.910
into the house, the old well, making sure
she is not followed.

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:47.340
She removes the planks from the top and sets
up a mock tea party, using the teacups to

00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:50.230
weigh down the picnic blanket and hide the
fact that the well was open.

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:54.510
Then, she goes back to the house, dangling
the key around for the hand to see, and LOUDLY

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:56.750
SAYS WHERE SHE’LL BE PLAYING.

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:59.740
This prompts the hand to go after her to try
to steal the key.

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:03.440
She places it in the center of the picnic
blanket, and the hand goes crashing down into

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:06.640
the depth of the well when it weighs down
the blanket, and she replaces the planks,

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:08.820
forever trapping the hand and the key at the
bottom of the well.

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:12.260
That night, as the summer ends, she hears
what she thinks is the mouse circus getting

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.070
ready for a performance upstairs.

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:18.170
Coraline’s story is, like many tales about
kids her age, a coming of age story, but her

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:20.620
transformation deals with much more nuanced
themes.

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:23.820
She goes through the stage that every kid
goes through, where their interests are maturing

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:26.710
and they have to learn to balance these interests,
something that you’re very used to doing

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:29.170
as an adult, but even then can be challenging
sometimes.

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:32.480
I think the biggest takeaway is that you have
to learn to appreciate the dull parts of life

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:35.540
because they make the exciting portions that
much better by comparison.

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:39.300
She also has to learn to grow up and face
fear in a mature way, taking examples from

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:43.860
her parents and ultimately using those experiences
to when her real mom and dad need her most.

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:47.350
So that’s the history of Coraline Jones,
but there’s so much more lore to unpack

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:51.240
with her greatest enemy, the Other Mother,
or the Beldam, so make sure you join my for

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.700
the next Horror History to learn all about
that.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:57.670
Your homework this lesson is to subscribe
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

00:15:57.670 --> 00:16:01.360
that deathbell for notifications and I’ll
see you in the next video.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:03.199
Assuming we both survive.

